<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Shah Massoud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1953–2001</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lion of Panjshir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Shah Massoud was an Afghan mujahideen commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamiat-e-islami">Jamiat-e Islami</a>, known as the Lion of Panjshir for defending the Panjshir valley against Soviet offensives in the 1980s. He was defence minister of the Islamic State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> from 1992 and later led the Northern Alliance against the Taliban. He was assassinated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qaeda">al-Qaeda</a> suicide bombers on 9 September 2001.</p></div>
